title The lift that kept its rung, the cost it priced in prose, and three guards that had been red in the dark
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, rota row N mod 5, send each finished increment
think Standfast first -- crux/REDS.md reads closed through %136, every row of the living range carrying its CLOSED companion, so the line is clear and constructive work may begin.
think The running thread's recommend named read_own_line as the head at four hundred and ninety-two, its three import widenings capabilities, carry, and cycle, all three already imported in the harness.
think Rota row 4 of 5 this lap (Earth - Mercury): the one-clock naming law, TWO_ROOMS, and the marked value. Two Rooms is the one that bit -- a widening cost described by a hand belongs in the vision room until a meter binds it, and this arc has already booked two reds for exactly that crossing.
think Measured before touching anything: forty-two rungs declare pub fn read_own_line and all forty-two hash identical, none of them below the fold line, since ladder_checks.rye imports none of the forty-two.
think The body reaches five names. capabilities, carry, and cycle stand private in each of the forty-two, which is the whole hundred and twenty-six the meter priced -- and the harness imports all three shared modules itself, so the lifted body reaches them there and pays nothing.
think The remaining two, queue_store and serve, already stand pub const on every one of the forty-two, both binding a single shared file -- one queue.rye and one serve.rye in the directory.
think That opened a real choice the meter cannot see. Importing queue.rye and serve.rye into the harness would let the lift drop its rung parameter as load_one did one lap earlier -- and would sink both rungs BELOW the fold line permanently, where a rung can never fold a body again.
think Chose the rung parameter. It costs one comptime argument and keeps two rungs foldable for every family they might yet join; the free-looking move charges the arc's future for convenience in the harness import list.
obs The fall formula corrected in REDS %136 got its first live use this lap and predicted 492 exactly: carry 68,851 -> 68,359, the difference 492 to the digit.
obs The queue reordered once read_own_line folded. look_again is the new head by cost -- twelve rungs of fifty-one lines returning 528 and opening nothing at all, of any kind. It is the largest genuinely free row the arc has been offered, and it sits behind three larger-looking rows only because it folds fewer rungs.
obs Four rows now sit at import-bindings-only -- elder_waits 504 (functions, so it genuinely costs), revoke_one and judge_outcome at 468, door_admits at 462 -- and each wants this lap's reading rather than its number: an import binding is free when the harness already holds the module, and costly when holding it would sink a rung.
think Then wrote the design essay the fold-line discovery seemed to deserve, and reaching for its opening measurement found the claim was never measured at all. Booked REDS %137: the sentence shipped into a witness's GREEN line and the operator card said the door was expensive; the two rungs hold three body lines each against a foldable corpus of 65,995.
think That is REDS %130's crossing a second time -- a fold cost described by a hand rather than read off the tree -- so a lantern firing twice became a loom: the visibility scan grew a sink mode that prices every rung's holding, with two RED legs on generated controls.
think The finding the meter gave that prose could not: the holdings spread three orders of magnitude, three lines to 3,901, so both "always keep the rung parameter" and "always import" are wrong and the door is priced before it is opened.
think Running the doorway guard against the new essay found it already RED, and RED with the essay removed too. Booked REDS %138: nine forward-facing pages stamped since 20260821 carry a Status naming a state rather than a room.
think Each of the nine read individually before its token was chosen -- Checkable for the measured-on-metal reads, Mixed where a page argues a shape while citing measurements it ran, Vision for the unseated proposal, Research for understanding for the dated model read.
obs The doorway guard runs from parity_ch01 and rishi_list_bound_witness rather than from the era suite or the Caravan choir, which is how a day of green rounds ran beside a red one. That half is named open rather than claimed closed -- seating it in a standing suite is a next lap's work.
think Then the dated-path guard, run for the same reason, was ALSO already RED with this lap's changes stashed -- the lost-reference census at 199 against a ceiling of 192. Booked REDS %139.
think Five of the seven were paths written test ! -f foundations/<stamp>_<slug>.md across two season witnesses -- proofs that a fossil was shed, counted as references that had gone missing. The exclusion list's own header already wrote the governing test, is this the field or the instrument, and warned that counting the instrument makes a meter rise as its proof gets stronger; it had only ever applied that test to filenames.
think An exclusion written as a list of NAMES cannot express a rule about GRAMMAR. A path's meaning depends on the sentence around it, and "! -f" is a different sentence from a citation, so the census takes a second grep pass anchored on the negation and subtracts per citing file rather than everywhere the name appears.
think The other two were genuine drift and were repointed by reading where the files stand: the 1024-round itinerary cited at 20260813-171050 rather than 20260812-171050 under date/20260812/, and the widening design read cited by a shortened basename.
think Three guards red before the lap began, none of them running from a standing suite -- that is the lap's real finding, and it is the same sentence this ledger's own founding wrote about reds living in a chat window that closes.
obs Closed the roster half in the same lap rather than deferring it: the era suite grew a twelfth rung carrying the doorway, the dated-path census, and the repointer, and reads GREEN at twelve. Every lap now hears all three.
obs The census landed back at exactly 192 against its 192 ceiling and the ceiling stayed put. A meter correction that removes a miscount earns no slack; seven references had genuinely drifted since the ceiling was set, and seven were closed.
